    <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
    <h1>Why does this exist</h1>
    <p class="thesis">I'm <b>Alan Lacroix</b>. I was born in Mexico City, grew up in Miami, and now I'm building a business in Mexico. When I started spending more time there, I realized I understood the country less than I thought. I wanted somewhere I could start with the facts and come to my own conclusions.</p>
    <p>Mexico Brief brings the numbers and the news together. It follows the official data, selects the developments worth paying attention to, explains the background, and separates what happened from what I think it means.</p>
    <p>I originally put this together for myself. Then family and friends started using it, so I made it public.</p>
    <p>For context, I look at Mexico partly from a US vantage point and partly as someone trying to build there. I'm interested in its political stability, economic growth, relationship with the United States, and position in technology, AI, private equity, payments, and entrepreneurship.</p>
    <p>I don't expect the numbers to settle every argument. I want them to make the argument better, and make Mexico easier to understand without reducing it to the loudest headline.</p>
    <p>Mexico is one of the world's largest economies, central to the United States' economic future, and still somehow a dependable first-knockout-round exit in the World Cup.</p>
